## 🧵 Stitch AI Prompt — Copy/Paste to Generate the Project

> Copy the entire prompt below and paste it into any AI coding assistant (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, Cursor, etc.) to scaffold the full project.

```
You are building a full-stack hackathon project called "MineGuard AI" — an AI-Based Smart Governance and Compliance Monitoring System for Coal Mines.

PROJECT OVERVIEW:
A digital platform that replaces manual paper-based compliance tracking in coal mining operations. It ensures mines adhere to statutory regulations (Safety, Environment, Production, Labour) using AI-powered analysis, automated workflows, and real-time dashboards. The system follows a 7-step workflow: Field Data Collection → Data Ingestion → AI Risk Analysis → AI Agent Investigation → Workflow & Action Management → Corrective Action Verification → Audit & Reporting.

TECH STACK:
- Frontend: Next.js 14 (App Router) + React + Tailwind CSS
- Charts: Recharts
- Maps: Leaflet + React-Leaflet + OpenStreetMap
- Backend: Next.js API Routes
- Database: SQLite via Prisma ORM
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4 API (or Google Gemini API)
- OCR: Tesseract.js (client-side)
- Auth: NextAuth.js with credential-based login
- File uploads: stored locally in /public/uploads

DATABASE SCHEMA (Prisma):
Create these models:
1. User — id, name, email, password, role (MINE_OFFICIAL | CORPORATE | REGULATOR | CONTRACTOR | INSPECTOR), mineId (optional)
2. Mine — id, name, location, latitude, longitude, subsidiaryName, riskScore, complianceScore
3. Inspection — id, mineId, inspectorId, type (SAFETY | ENVIRONMENT | PRODUCTION | LABOUR), zone, observations, severity (CRITICAL | MAJOR | MINOR), status (PENDING | IN_PROGRESS | COMPLETED | REVIEWED), photos (JSON array of file paths), gpsLat, gpsLng, createdAt
4. Violation — id, inspectionId, mineId, regulationType, description, severity, status (OPEN | ASSIGNED | IN_PROGRESS | SUBMITTED | VERIFIED | CLOSED), assignedTo, deadline, escalationLevel (0-4), aiAnalysis (JSON), createdAt
5. CorrectiveAction — id, violationId, submittedBy, actionDescription, evidencePhotos (JSON), verificationStatus (PENDING | APPROVED | REWORK), aiVerificationNotes, submittedAt, verifiedAt
6. AuditLog — id, userId, action, entityType, entityId, details (JSON), timestamp
7. Alert — id, userId, violationId, message, type (REMINDER | ESCALATION | RISK_ALERT), isRead, createdAt
8. ComplianceRule — id, category (SAFETY | ENVIRONMENT | PRODUCTION | LABOUR), ruleCode, title, description, authority (DGMS | CPCB | LABOUR_DEPT)

Seed the database with:
- 5 mines with realistic Indian coal mine names and locations (Jharia, Singrauli, Korba, Talcher, Raniganj) with lat/lng coordinates
- 20+ compliance rules across all 4 categories
- 50+ historical inspections with varied results
- 15+ violations in various statuses
- 5 users (one per role)
- Historical data spanning 6 months for trend charts

PAGES TO BUILD:

1. LOGIN PAGE (/) — Role-based login with demo buttons for each role (Mine Official, Corporate, Regulator, Contractor, Inspector). Dark theme, modern glassmorphism design.

2. INSPECTOR: NEW INSPECTION (/inspection/new) — Mobile-responsive form with:
   - Mine selector, zone input, inspection type dropdown
   - Observation textarea
   - Severity selector (Critical/Major/Minor)
   - Photo upload with camera capture option
   - Auto-capture GPS coordinates (use browser Geolocation API)
   - Auto-capture timestamp
   - Submit button that sends to API, which then calls AI for auto-classification

3. MINE OFFICIAL DASHBOARD (/dashboard/mine) — Shows:
   - Compliance score donut chart (compliant/pending/violated/overdue)
   - Upcoming deadlines list (next 7 days)
   - Active violations table (sortable by severity) with status badges
   - Recent inspections feed with timeline
   - Quick action buttons (New Inspection, Log Violation, View Map)
   - AI risk alerts panel

4. CORPORATE DASHBOARD (/dashboard/corporate) — Shows:
   - Multi-mine bar chart ranking compliance scores
   - 6-month trend line chart of compliance across all mines
   - AI risk alerts panel highlighting predicted high-risk mines
   - Escalation summary (overdue violations per mine)
   - Mine map with color-coded pins (green=safe, yellow=moderate, red=high-risk)
   - KPI cards: total inspections, open violations, avg resolution time, compliance %

5. REGULATORY DASHBOARD (/dashboard/regulator) — Shows:
   - All mines compliance overview table
   - Violation history with filters (by mine, severity, date, regulation type)
   - Audit trail log (read-only, shows every action with timestamps)
   - Download buttons for compliance reports (generate on-demand)
   - Submission tracker (on-time vs overdue statutory submissions)

6. CONTRACTOR PORTAL (/dashboard/contractor) — Shows:
   - Assigned tasks list with deadlines and countdown timers
   - Task detail view with violation info
   - Evidence submission form (upload photos + description of action taken)
   - Compliance status tracker for their assignments

7. VIOLATIONS PAGE (/violations) — List all violations with AI analysis details. Click a violation to see the AI Agent's 6-step reasoning (Observe, Retrieve, Reason, Decide, Act, Verify).

8. GIS MAP PAGE (/map) — Full-screen Leaflet map showing all mines. Each mine is a pin colored by risk level. Click a pin to see mine compliance score, recent violations, and risk details in a popup.

9. REPORTS PAGE (/reports) — Select a mine and date range. Click "Generate Report" to have AI create a compliance report. Display the report and offer PDF download.

API ROUTES TO BUILD:

1. POST /api/inspections — Create inspection, auto-classify with AI, check for violations
2. GET /api/inspections — List inspections with filters
3. GET /api/violations — List violations with filters
4. POST /api/ai/analyze — Run AI risk analysis on a mine's data
5. POST /api/ai/agent — Run AI Agent investigation on a specific violation (returns 6-step reasoning)
6. POST /api/ai/verify — AI verification of submitted corrective action
7. POST /api/ai/report — AI-generated compliance report
8. POST /api/actions — Submit corrective action with evidence
9. GET /api/alerts — Get alerts for current user
10. GET /api/audit-log — Get audit trail (regulator view)
11. GET /api/dashboard/mine — Aggregated data for mine dashboard
12. GET /api/dashboard/corporate — Aggregated data for corporate dashboard

AI INTEGRATION:
Use OpenAI's chat completions API (or Gemini). Create a lib/prompts.js file with all prompt templates. The AI Agent should follow this reasoning loop:
- OBSERVE: Read the violation data
- RETRIEVE: Match against compliance rules in the knowledge base
- REASON: Analyze severity considering mine history and contractor track record
- DECIDE: Recommend specific corrective actions
- ACT: Set assignments, deadlines, and escalation triggers
- VERIFY: Define what "resolved" looks like

ESCALATION LOGIC:
Implement an escalation engine that checks violation deadlines:
- Due today → Reminder to assignee
- 2 days overdue → Notify supervisor
- 5 days overdue → Escalate to mine manager  
- 7+ days overdue → Alert corporate + regulator
Run this as a check on every relevant API call (or use a cron-like background check).

UI DESIGN REQUIREMENTS:
- Dark theme with a professional color scheme (dark navy background, teal/green accents for safe, amber for warnings, red for critical)
- Glassmorphism cards with subtle backdrop blur
- Smooth animations and transitions
- Fully responsive (must look great on mobile for the inspector form)
- Status badges with colors: Green (Compliant/Closed), Yellow (Pending/In Progress), Red (Violated/Critical), Blue (Assigned)
- Use Google Font "Inter" for typography

IMPORTANT INSTRUCTIONS:
1. Seed the database with enough realistic data to make dashboards look impressive during demo
2. Every AI call should have a loading state with a nice animation
3. The AI Agent reasoning should be displayed step-by-step (like a thinking process) on the violation detail page
4. The audit log should capture EVERY action (inspection created, violation detected, task assigned, action submitted, etc.)
5. Make the GIS map interactive — clicking mines should show rich popups
6. The compliance score should be calculated as: (compliant_items / total_items) × 100
7. Add micro-animations on cards, charts, and status changes for a polished feel

Generate the complete project with all files. Start with the Prisma schema, then seed data, then API routes, then pages. Make sure everything is connected and working end-to-end.
```

